---
/*
  Studios / Church Studio (/studios/church-studio) - Persuade surface, first entry
  in the Studios product line (fixed-structure, industry-specific builds).
  Established-world extension of the homepage's "Grounded Workshop" - no new world,
  no concept roll. Copy source: pages/church-studio-copy.md (drafted, implemented
  verbatim). Reshaped 2026-08-07 (Fable pass, Sweven services page as structural
  reference): every section carries a distinct archetype - split hero with the Haw
  Branch homepage as proof imagery, asymmetric two-column qualify, page-index +
  sticky screenshot rail, ONE earned single-column moment (How It's Different),
  a full-width timeline stat band, a dominant-image proof row, split pricing,
  split FAQ, and the dark closing with the dedicated inquiry form on Dark Card.
  Eyebrow appears once (hero) - the per-section eyebrow scaffold was removed as
  an AI tell. See .impeccable/surfaces/src-pages-studios.md.
*/
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

// The fixed 8-page structure every Church Studio site ships with.
const pages = [
  { name: "Home", job: "The front door. Who you are, who this is for, and why it matters, in one screen." },
  { name: "Plan Your Visit", job: "Answers every question a first-time guest actually has before they show up." },
  { name: "About", job: "Your story, your beliefs, your leadership. Where trust gets built." },
  { name: "Kids", job: "Safety, check-in, and what to expect. The page anxious parents read first." },
  { name: "Messages", job: "Your current series and message archive." },
  { name: "Events", job: "What’s happening and when." },
  { name: "Give", job: "A clear, guilt-free link to your giving platform." },
  { name: "Contact", job: "Address, phone, map, and a way to reach your team." },
];

const faqs = [
  {
    q: "How is this different from a full Proudly Sites project?",
    a: "Church Studio uses a fixed page structure and layout system built specifically for churches, instead of a fully custom design process. You still get original copy and a site that looks like your church, just built on a faster timeline.",
  },
  {
    q: "Do you write the copy?",
    a: "Yes. I’ll ask the right questions during onboarding, your service length, what to wear, your kids’ check-in process, whether you livestream, and write copy that sounds like your pastor, not a denominational press release.",
  },
  {
    q: "Can I still link out to Planning Center, Church Center, or our giving platform?",
    a: "Yes. Church Studio is built to work alongside the tools you already use, not replace them.",
  },
  {
    q: "What if we need more than the eight pages?",
    a: "The eight-page structure covers what most churches need. If you have a real case for more, a students ministry, multiple locations, let’s talk. It may move you toward the top of the pricing range or into a standard Proudly Sites project instead.",
  },
  {
    q: "Who updates the site after launch?",
    a: "You will, or whoever on your team you choose. The site is built so your team can update service times, events, and series art without touching code.",
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Church Studio · Proudly Sites"
  description="A faster, purpose-built website process for churches: a fixed eight-page structure proven to turn first-time visitors into first-time guests, live in one to two weeks."
>
  <section class="section studio-hero">
    <!--
      THESIS: a purpose-built process for churches sells on the fixed, proven structure shown through a real build, not asserted; refuse the generic agency service page AND the single-column left-text scaffold.
      OWN-WORLD: the homepage's Grounded Workshop, inherited whole - Warm Cream ground, Espresso Black close, Playfair headings on Lato text, Honey Gold decorating only, one Burnt Terracotta stacked-shadow CTA.
      STORY: a pastor deciding on a rebuild sees a real church site in the first viewport, scans exactly what the eight pages do beside real template screens, checks price and timeline, then starts an inquiry without leaving the page.
      FIRST VIEWPORT: split hero - promise H1 + lead + anchor CTA left, the Haw Branch homepage right. Proof leads.
      FORM: long-scroll product page where every section carries a different archetype (split hero, asymmetric qualify, index + screenshot rail, one earned minimal beat, stat band, dominant-image proof, split pricing, split FAQ, dark ask). Structural reference: Sweven services page grammar, rebuilt on this world's tokens.
    -->
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <h1>A Website Built for Someone Deciding Whether to Walk In</h1>
      <p class="lead">Proudly Sites builds custom websites for growing businesses. Church Studio is different &mdash; a faster, purpose-built process for churches, with a fixed structure proven to turn first-time visitors into first-time guests.</p>
      <a class="primary-button hero-cta" href="#inquiry">Start Your Church Studio Project</a>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-visual">
      <img src="/images/haw-branch-home.jpeg" alt="The Haw Branch Church homepage: a warm photo of worship with the headline 'There's a seat for you Sunday.'" width="1600" height="896" fetchpriority="high" />
      <p class="visual-cite">Haw Branch Church &mdash; a Church Studio build</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="surface-white">
    <section class="section who">
      <div class="who-grid">
        <header class="who-head">
          <h2 class="rv">Built for Churches Ready to Take Their Website Seriously</h2>
          <p class="section-intro rv">Church Studio works best for:</p>
        </header>
        <ul class="qualifiers stagger">
          <li>One pastor or a small team making the decision &mdash; not a committee</li>
          <li>A church that already has real momentum: consistent attendance, active ministries, a clear identity</li>
          <li>Leadership who wants the site to serve first-time visitors, not just members</li>
          <li>Churches who already use Planning Center, Church Center, or a giving platform and want the site to work alongside them, not replace them</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <p class="disqualifier rv">If your church is just getting started or design decisions run through a large board, a slower and more custom process &mdash; or simply more time before a rebuild &mdash; usually serves you better.</p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <section class="section included">
    <header class="included-head rv">
      <h2>One Structure. Proven to Work.</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">Every Church Studio site includes eight pages, each with a specific job:</p>
    </header>
    <div class="included-grid">
      <div class="included-list">
        <ul class="page-index stagger">
          {pages.map((p) => (
            <li class="page-row">
              <span class="page-name">{p.name}</span>
              <span class="page-job">{p.job}</span>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
        <p class="included-close rv">The layouts are set. The structure is proven. What we build together is the words, the photos, and the details that make it unmistakably your church.</p>
      </div>
      <aside class="included-visuals">
        <figure class="shot rv">
          <img src="/images/haw-branch-sunday.jpeg" alt="The Haw Branch Plan Your Visit page walking a first-time guest through Sunday morning, hour by hour" loading="lazy" width="1600" height="808" />
        </figure>
        <figure class="shot rv">
          <img src="/images/haw-branch-answers.jpeg" alt="The Haw Branch site answering the honest questions a first-time guest actually has" loading="lazy" width="1600" height="893" />
        </figure>
        <figcaption class="visual-cite rv">From the Haw Branch Church build</figcaption>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="surface-white">
    <section class="section different">
      <h2 class="rv">Faster Because the Guesswork Is Gone</h2>
      <p class="body-copy rv">A standard Proudly Sites project starts from a blank page &mdash; full custom design, full strategy build, three to six weeks. Church Studio starts from a structure that already works for churches, refined across real projects and built around one question:</p>
      <blockquote class="pullquote rv">Would a first-time visitor feel confident enough to attend after two minutes on your homepage?</blockquote>
      <p class="body-copy rv">That means less time spent exploring layouts, more time spent getting your words, your photos, and your service details right. You&rsquo;re not getting less craft. You&rsquo;re getting a process built specifically for what a church website needs to do.</p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <div class="surface-oat">
    <section class="section timeline">
      <h2 class="rv">Live in One<br />to Two Weeks</h2>
      <p class="body-copy rv">Most Church Studio projects go from kickoff to launch in one to two weeks. The pace comes from the fixed structure &mdash; we&rsquo;re not deciding what pages you need or how they&rsquo;re laid out, so we can move straight to making them yours.</p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <div class="surface-white">
    <section class="section proof">
      <div class="proof-row">
        <figure class="proof-visual rv">
          <img src="/images/haw-branch-next.jpeg" alt="The Haw Branch next-steps section and dark closing footer, inviting a returning guest to join First Step" loading="lazy" width="1600" height="884" />
        </figure>
        <div class="proof-copy">
          <h2 class="rv">See It In Action</h2>
          <p class="proof-client rv">Haw Branch Church</p>
          <p class="proof-caption rv">A Church Studio build currently in progress. Once live, this section will show the finished site alongside a short note on what it solved for their first-time visitors.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <section class="section pricing">
    <div class="pricing-grid">
      <div class="pricing-lead">
        <h2 class="price rv">$700&ndash;$950</h2>
        <p class="section-intro rv">Every Church Studio project starts at $700. Two things move the price up within that range:</p>
        <p class="included-close rv">A single-campus church with a typical ministry list lands at the low end. Reach out and I&rsquo;ll give you an exact number based on your church.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="factor-index stagger">
        <li class="page-row">
          <span class="page-name">Number of ministries</span>
          <span class="page-job">More distinct ministries beyond the core structure means more content to organize and present clearly.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="page-row">
          <span class="page-name">Multisite</span>
          <span class="page-job">If your church has more than one campus, each location needs its own service times, address, and directions built into the site.</span>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="surface-white">
    <section class="section faq">
      <div class="faq-grid">
        <h2 class="faq-title rv">FAQ</h2>
        <div class="faq-list stagger">
          {faqs.map((f) => (
            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary>{f.q}</summary>
              <p>{f.a}</p>
            </details>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <section class="studio-close" id="inquiry">
    <h2>Ready to Give First-Time Visitors<br />a Reason to Come Back</h2>
    <p class="close-lead">Tell me about your church and I&rsquo;ll come back with an exact number and a start date. You&rsquo;ll work with me directly, from the first message through launch.</p>

    <div class="inquiry-card">
      <form id="studio-form" action="https://api.web3forms.com/submit" method="POST">
        <!-- TODO: replace with the real Web3Forms access key (public, safe to commit). -->
        <input type="hidden" name="access_key" value="YOUR_WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY" />
        <input type="hidden" name="subject" value="New Church Studio inquiry from proudlysites.com" />
        <input type="hidden" name="from_name" value="Proudly Sites — Church Studio" />
        <!-- Honeypot: real people leave this untouched; bots trip it. -->
        <input type="checkbox" name="botcheck" class="hp" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" aria-hidden="true" />

        <div class="field-row">
          <div class="field">
            <label for="sf-name">Name <span class="req" aria-hidden="true">*</span></label>
            <input id="sf-name" name="name" type="text" required autocomplete="name" placeholder="Your name" />
          </div>
          <div class="field">
            <label for="sf-email">Email <span class="req" aria-hidden="true">*</span></label>
            <input id="sf-email" name="email" type="email" required autocomplete="email" placeholder="you@yourchurch.com" />
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="field">
          <label for="sf-church">Church name <span class="req" aria-hidden="true">*</span></label>
          <input id="sf-church" name="church" type="text" required autocomplete="organization" placeholder="Your church" />
        </div>

        <div class="field">
          <label for="sf-message">Message <span class="req" aria-hidden="true">*</span></label>
          <textarea id="sf-message" name="message" rows="5" required placeholder="Tell me about your church, your current site, and what's prompting the rebuild."></textarea>
        </div>

        <p class="form-error" id="studio-form-error" role="alert" hidden>
          Something went wrong sending that. Email me directly at
          <a href="mailto:alex@proudlysites.com">alex@proudlysites.com</a> and I&rsquo;ll get right back to you.
        </p>

        <button type="submit" class="primary-button form-submit">Start Your Church Studio Project</button>
        <p class="form-note">You&rsquo;ll hear back from me personally.</p>
      </form>

      <div class="form-success" id="studio-form-success" role="status" tabindex="-1" hidden>
        <span class="success-mark" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12" /></svg>
        </span>
        <h3>Message sent</h3>
        <p>Thanks, it&rsquo;s on its way. You&rsquo;ll hear back from me personally.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* Route-specific composition for the Church Studio product page. Tokens + chrome
     are global; the world is inherited from the homepage and the services cluster.
     Section grammar: every section a distinct archetype; single-column reserved
     for the one How It's Different beat. */

  .surface-white { background: var(--white); }
  .surface-oat { background: var(--oat); }

  /* ---- Shared section type ---- */
  .section h2 {
    font-family: "Playfair Display", Georgia, serif;
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(28px, 3.4vw, 40px);
    line-height: 1.14;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    text-wrap: balance;
    margin: 0 0 22px;
    max-width: 22ch;
  }
  .section-intro,
  .body-copy {
    font-size: 20px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin: 0 0 24px;
    max-width: 40rem;
  }

  /* ---- Screenshot framing (shared: hero, rail, proof) ---- */
  .hero-visual img,
  .shot img,
  .proof-visual img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 10px;
  }
  .visual-cite {
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #6d635c;
    margin: 14px 0 0;
  }

  /* ---- Hero: split, proof leads ---- */
  .section.studio-hero {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 0.94fr 1.06fr;
    gap: clamp(36px, 5vw, 76px);
    align-items: center;
    max-width: 1240px;
    padding-top: clamp(48px, 6vw, 92px);
    padding-bottom: clamp(48px, 6vw, 96px);
  }
  .studio-hero h1 {
    font-family: "Playfair Display", Georgia, serif;
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(32px, 3.9vw, 50px);
    line-height: 1.06;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    text-wrap: balance;
    margin: 0 0 22px;
    max-width: 18ch;
  }
  .studio-hero .lead {
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin: 0 0 32px;
    max-width: 34rem;
  }
  .hero-visual {
    background: var(--sand);
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: clamp(18px, 2vw, 28px);
  }
  .hero-visual .visual-cite { margin-top: 12px; }

  /* ---- Who It's For: asymmetric two-column, disqualifier band below ---- */
  .who-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 0.9fr 1.1fr;
    gap: clamp(36px, 5vw, 88px);
    align-items: start;
  }
  .who-head { position: sticky; top: 110px; }
  .who-head .section-intro { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .qualifiers {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 6px 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .qualifiers li {
    position: relative;
    padding: 22px 0 22px 28px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--espresso);
  }
  .qualifiers li::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: 4px;
    top: 32px;
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--gold);
  }
  .disqualifier {
    font-family: "Playfair Display", Georgia, serif;
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(18px, 2vw, 22px);
    line-height: 1.55;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin: clamp(40px, 5vw, 64px) 0 0;
    max-width: 44rem;
  }

  /* ---- What's Included: page index + sticky screenshot rail ---- */
  .included-head { max-width: 700px; }
  .included-head .section-intro { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .included-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.05fr 0.95fr;
    gap: clamp(36px, 5vw, 80px);
    align-items: start;
    margin-top: clamp(28px, 3.5vw, 48px);
  }
  .page-index {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0 0 36px;
    padding: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .page-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(120px, 170px) 1fr;
    gap: clamp(16px, 2.5vw, 40px);
    align-items: baseline;
    padding: 17px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .page-name {
    font-family: "Playfair Display", Georgia, serif;
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(18px, 1.8vw, 22px);
    line-height: 1.2;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--espresso);
  }
  .page-job {
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--muted);
    max-width: 52ch;
  }
  .included-close {
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--espresso);
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 42rem;
  }
  .included-visuals {
    position: sticky;
    top: 96px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 18px;
    background: var(--sand);
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: clamp(18px, 2vw, 26px);
  }
  .included-visuals .shot { margin: 0; }
  .included-visuals .visual-cite { margin: 0; }

  /* ---- How It's Different: THE single-column minimal beat ---- */
  .section.different { max-width: 820px; }
  .pullquote {
    font-family: "Playfair Display", Georgia, serif;
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(24px, 2.8vw, 32px);
    line-height: 1.4;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--espresso);
    margin: 36px 0;
    padding-left: 26px;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--gold);
    max-width: 30ch;
  }

  /* ---- Timeline: full-width stat band on Oat ---- */
  .section.timeline {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto 1fr;
    gap: clamp(32px, 6vw, 110px);
    align-items: center;
    padding-top: clamp(56px, 7vw, 96px);
    padding-bottom: clamp(56px, 7vw, 96px);
  }
  .section.timeline h2 {
    font-size: clamp(36px, 4.6vw, 60px);
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .section.timeline .body-copy { margin: 0; max-width: 36rem; }

  /* ---- Proof: dominant image feature row ---- */
  .proof-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.35fr 0.65fr;
    gap: clamp(32px, 4.5vw, 72px);
    align-items: center;
  }
  .proof-visual {
    margin: 0;
    background: var(--sand);
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: clamp(18px, 2.2vw, 30px);
  }
  .proof-copy h2 { margin-bottom: 18px; }
  .proof-client {
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #6d635c;
    margin: 0 0 14px;
  }
  .proof-caption {
    font-family: "Playfair Display", Georgia, serif;
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(20px, 2.1vw, 25px);
    line-height: 1.45;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--espresso);
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 32ch;
  }

  /* ---- Pricing: split ---- */
  .pricing-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 0.9fr 1.1fr;
    gap: clamp(36px, 5vw, 88px);
    align-items: start;
  }
  .pricing-lead h2.price {
    font-size: clamp(40px, 5vw, 64px);
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }
  .pricing-lead .included-close { margin-top: 8px; }
  .factor-index {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 10px 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .factor-index .page-row {
    grid-template-columns: minmax(140px, 200px) 1fr;
    padding: clamp(22px, 2.6vw, 30px) 0;
  }

  /* ---- FAQ: split (label left, disclosure right) ---- */
  .faq-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 0.35fr 1fr;
    gap: clamp(36px, 5vw, 88px);
    align-items: start;
  }
  .faq-title { position: sticky; top: 110px; margin: 0; }
  .faq-list { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .faq-item { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .faq-item summary {
    position: relative;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
    padding: 22px 44px 22px 0;
    font-family: "Playfair Display", Georgia, serif;
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(18px, 2vw, 22px);
    line-height: 1.35;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--espresso);
  }
  .faq-item summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
  .faq-item summary::after {
    content: "+";
    position: absolute;
    right: 6px;
    top: 50%;
    transform: translateY(-50%);
    font-size: 22px;
    font-weight: 300;
    color: #6d635c;
    transition: transform 0.25s ease;
  }
  .faq-item[open] summary::after { transform: translateY(-50%) rotate(45deg); }
  .faq-item p {
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0 44px 24px 0;
    max-width: 62ch;
  }

  /* ---- Dark closing with the dedicated inquiry form ---- */
  .studio-close {
    background: var(--espresso);
    color: #fff;
    text-align: center;
    padding: clamp(90px, 10vw, 130px) 24px clamp(90px, 10vw, 120px);
  }
  .studio-close h2 {
    font: 500 clamp(30px, 3.4vw, 40px)/1.15 "Playfair Display", serif;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    margin: 0 0 22px;
  }
  .close-lead {
    max-width: 610px;
    margin: 0 auto 44px;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.72);
    line-height: 1.6;
    font-size: 20px;
  }

  /* Dark Card inquiry surface (DESIGN.md: cards inset into Espresso Black use
     Dark Card with a subtle translucent white hairline). */
  .inquiry-card {
    max-width: 560px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    text-align: left;
    background: var(--dark-card);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.14);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 36px;
  }

  .field { margin-bottom: 18px; }
  .field-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 16px; }
  .field label {
    display: block;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);
    margin-bottom: 7px;
  }
  .req { color: var(--terracotta); }

  .field input,
  .field textarea {
    width: 100%;
    font-family: inherit;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--espresso);
    background: var(--cream);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
